# Echocasting Symposium ({4}{U}{U}): "Target player creates a token that's a copy of target creature you control" (CR 707.2) and
# paradigm (CR 702.192a). Turn 1: Bot1 pays with Black Lotus (three blue), Mox Sapphire, Mox Jet and Mox Ruby and targets Bot2 and
# its own Ornithopter: Bot2, not Bot1, creates and controls the Ornithopter token. Bot2's token is not a creature Bot1 controls, so
# Bot1 can only copy its own. Turn 3: Bot1 accepts the free copy of the exiled spell and targets itself: it gets a token too.
# Turn 5: the copy is declined, so nothing more happens.

[Bot1 Deck]
Ornithopter
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Echocasting Symposium
Island x2
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Echocasting Symposium.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Token = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
? Exile = Echocasting Symposium
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Decline
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Exile = Echocasting Symposium
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
